    "body": "## Overview\n\nStop calling `cudaProfilerStart`/`cudaProfilerStop` while `torch.profiler` owns CUPTI for `vllm bench forward --profile-dir`.\n\nPR #61692 added both mechanisms around the same graph replays. The new H200 Benchmarks CLI test passed once in PR build #95582, then failed in daily builds #95663 and #95703 on two different hosts with an empty trace plus `bufferCompleted called with unknown buffer`. This keeps the CUDA profiler markers for the Nsight Systems path (without `--profile-dir`) and lets `torch.profiler` exclusively own CUPTI for the JSON/Perfetto path.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pytest tests/benchmarks/test_forward_cli.py -k 'profile_summary or torch_profile_does_not_toggle_cuda_profiler' -q` — 2 passed\n- `pre-commit run --files vllm/benchmarks/forward/profile.py tests/benchmarks/test_forward_cli.py` — passed\n- Exact H200 Benchmarks CLI build [#95708](https://buildkite.com/vllm/ci/builds/95708) — 203 passed, including `test_profile_summary`, `test_torch_profile_does_not_toggle_cuda_profiler`, and the real `test_bench_forward` profile path\n\n## AI assistance\n\nAI assistance was used to investigate the CI failures and prepare this patch. Human review is required before merge.\n",
